To include the ABOR and CWD commands in the appropriate places in the sequence of client requests, we can add the CWD command after the PWD command to change the directory, and the ABOR command can be placed before the QUIT command to abort any ongoing operation, if necessary.

Here’s the modified sequence of client requests:

```
USER anonymous
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
CWD /desired/directory  # Specify the desired directory here
PORT 127,0,0,1,152,193
LIST
ABOR  # This command can be used to abort the LIST command if needed
QUIT
```

Make sure to replace `/desired/directory` with the actual path you want to change to. The ABOR command is optional and may be included if you want to ensure that any ongoing data transfer is aborted before quitting

